// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeDockerImage(path: "/recipes/docker-image", title: "Build a Docker image — Recipes", description: "1.") {
    RecipeShell("Build a Docker image", summary: "1. Add a `Dockerfile`. The first stage installs `wf` and builds the site; the second serves it with nginx:     ```dockerfile FROM debian:stable-slim AS build RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y curl ca-certificates RUN curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent/master/install.sh | bash WORKDIR /site COPY . . RUN /root/.webfluent/bin/wf build     FROM nginx:alpine COPY --from=build /site/build /usr/share/nginx/html ```  2. To use the settings from [Serve with nginx](/recipes/serve-with-nginx), copy them into the second stage as `/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf`. When TLS ends in front of the container, write `listen 80;` in place of the `listen 443 ssl http2;` line. 3. Build and run the image:     ```bash docker build -t site . docker run -p 8080:80 site ```  **Verify it:** open `http://localhost:8080` and a deep link, and check the headers with `curl -I http://localhost:8080/`.", outputs: [], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Check a deploy", to: "/recipes/check-a-deploy"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to Cloudflare Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-cloudflare-pages"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to GitHub Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-github-pages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/docker-image.md", how: false, hasVariations: false) {
    }
}
